From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpl: the annealer's question as a packing problem

toPackingProblem() states what an annealer is asked: its sequence-pair
macros inside its outline, each with every shape the annealer can give
it (SoftMacro::resizeRandomly's area per width interval), fixed ones
where they are; terminals and empty macros take no room. The test checks
that every shape the annealer produces is one the problem allows.

Not upstreamed; retires at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

---
